# Continue before a write still reaches the next iteration

Verifies a `continue` is a loop backedge, not an exit. The body writes `2cm`
and continues on the first iteration, so the second iteration reads the stored
centimeter value and prints `21mm`.

>>> source
let a: int[] = [10mm]

for (i in 0..2) {
    if (i == 0) {
        a[0] = 2cm
        continue
    }
    print(a[0] + 1mm)
}

<<< stdout
21mm

<<< stderr
